/-!
# KFG: scaled Gaussian coefficients and scaled linear-combination expressions

Dyadic Gaussian data are stored as Gaussian integers with a per-role scale `2^{-e}`.  Aligning
two roles of different scales multiplies one stream by `2^d`, which costs `O(w + d)` per entry
through the ruler shift `Ex.shl` (a linear expression).

* `SC`: a scaled coefficient `c · 2^d` with `c ∈ {-1,0,1}²` (`SC.Ok`), acting by `smulS`.
* `tsE c d r = (c · top r) ≪ 2^d`, `lsE l = Σ tsE`: linear register expressions
  (`lsE_eval`, `lsE_bnd`, `lsE_lin`, `lsE_size`).
* `push_lsE`: one push of such a combination, at cost `(5 |l| + 2) · 2000 · (w + D + e + 2)`.
* `M2S`: a `2 × 2` matrix of scaled coefficients; `lin2S p q x y = p·x + q·y`; `lin2S_bnd`.
-/

